<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 413 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artas was a Messapian ruler in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in the late fifth century BCE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a>, in 413 BCE he renewed an old friendship with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and supplied 150 Messapian javelin-men to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicilian-expedition">Athenian expedition to Sicily</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demosthenes-general">Demosthenes</a>. He is one of the few Messapian rulers named in Greek sources.</p></div>
